# Audio Assets Management
<version>1.0.0</version>

## Context
- When implementing new sound effects in the game
- When adding audio feedback for game events
- When modifying existing audio implementation
- When expanding audio support for new game features

## Requirements
- Check the temp_audio directory for available sound effects before implementing new audio features
- Use "The Essential Retro Video Game Sound Effects Collection" by Juhani Junkala from temp_audio
- Map appropriate sound effects to game actions based on their semantic meaning
- Implement both MP3 and OGG formats for cross-browser compatibility
- Document any new sound effects used in the SPECS.md file

## Examples

<example>
```typescript
// Good: Checking and using available audio assets
export class SoundEffectsManager {
  constructor(scene: Phaser.Scene) {
    // Load assets from temp_audio directory
    scene.load.audio('hit', [
      'assets/audio/hit.mp3',
      'assets/audio/hit.ogg'
    ]);
    
    // Map game actions to existing sound effects
    this.actionSoundMap = {
      playerHit: 'hit',
      enemyDeath: 'death',
      towerBuild: 'build',
      soulCollect: 'collect'
    };
  }
  
  playActionSound(action: string): void {
    const soundKey = this.actionSoundMap[action];
    if (soundKey) {
      // Play the pre-mapped sound from temp_audio collection
      this.audioManager.playSound(soundKey);
    }
  }
}
```
This example properly uses the pre-downloaded audio collection, ensuring consistent sound effects throughout the game.
</example>

<example type="invalid">
```typescript
// Bad: Creating arbitrary sound effects without checking available assets
export class BadSoundImplementation {
  constructor(scene: Phaser.Scene) {
    // Creating arbitrary sound keys without checking temp_audio
    scene.load.audio('random_laser', 'assets/audio/laser.mp3');
    scene.load.audio('custom_explosion', 'assets/audio/boom.mp3');
    
    // No mapping to existing effects
    this.sounds = {
      attack: 'random_laser',
      destroy: 'custom_explosion'
    };
  }
  
  playSound(type: string): void {
    // Using arbitrary sounds not from the temp_audio collection
    this.scene.sound.play(this.sounds[type]);
  }
}
```
This implementation ignores the existing audio collection in temp_audio, creating inconsistency in sound effects and potentially causing missing assets issues.
</example>

## Phaser-Specific Notes

1. When loading audio files from temp_audio, ensure proper asset path configuration:
   ```typescript
   // During preload phase
   this.load.setPath('assets/audio/');
   this.load.audio('hit', ['hit.mp3', 'hit.ogg']);
   ```

2. Common sound effects and their semantic mapping:
   - Combat: 'hit', 'shoot', 'death'
   - Building: 'build', 'collect'
   - UI: 'ui_click', 'ui_hover'
   - Game events: 'wave_start'
   - Ambient: 'ambient_wind', 'ambient_crowd' 